source items (e.g. 7), but the pattern MUST be the same:\n   105→first all `Sources(QUESTION i)` items, then one `Union(...)`, one or more `Filter(...)` based on the number of unique products, one `Sort(...)`,\n   106→and finally one “write result” item.\n   107→\n   108→You should use this TODO list as the execution plan and mark items as completed as you progress.\n   109→\n   110→After all `Sources(QUESTION i)` tasks are done, you MUST rewrite the TODO list:\n   111→- Replace the generic filter items with one `Filter(<product name>)` per discovered product (the count of Filter items must equal the number of products).\n   112→- Keep `Sort(filtered)` and the final write step after those filter items.\n   113→\n   114→Example refreshed TODO after finding 3 products:\n   115→TODO List\n   116→- [ ] Filter(Product Alpha)\n   117→- [ ] Filter(Product Beta)\n   118→- [ ] Filter(Product Gamma)\n   119→- [ ] Sort(filtered)\n   120→- [ ] Write result to result.yaml\n   121→\n   122→**Progress logging pattern (few-shot)**\n   123→- After EVERY action item, add an explicit “Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json” item (and mark it done once you rewrite and overwrite the file).\n   124→- This enforces a rhythm of: do a step → record progress → rewrite TODO → update `new-product.json` → next step.\n   125→- Sample pattern the model should mirror:\n   126→  - [ ] Consider how to update todos based on products\n   127→  - [ ] Sources(QUESTION 1)\n   128→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   129→  - [ ] Sources(QUESTION 2)\n   130→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   131→  - [ ] Sources(QUESTION 3)\n   132→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   133→  - [ ] Union(all source results)\n   134→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   135→  - [ ] Filter(Product 1)\n   136→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   137→  - [ ] Filter(Product 2)\n   138→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   139→  - [ ] Filter(Product 3)\n   140→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   141→  - [ ] Sort(filtered)\n   142→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   143→  - [ ] Write result to new-product.json\n   144→  - [ ] Record progress, rewrite todo, update new-product.json\n   145→\n   146→**Final output format (what you actually return):**\n   147→\n   148→- Return a **JSON array** of products, sorted from most to least interesting.\n   149→- Each entry MUST have the following fields:\n   150→\n   151→  ```json\n   152→  [\n   153→    {\n   154→      \"name\": \"<product name>\",\n   155→      \"url\": \"<official homepage>\",\n   156→      \"description\": \"1–3 sentence summary of what this product does, focused on the developer / AI-coding use case.\",\n   157→      \"release_date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n   158→      \"category\": \"<short label, e.g. \\\"AI IDE\\\", \\\"AI coding CLI\\\", \\\"code agent\\\", \\\"workflow agent\\\">\",\n   159→      \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\", \"Show HN\", \"Reddit\", \"X\"],\n   160→      \"community_quotes\": [\n   161→        \"<short quote from community describing what people like or notice>\",\n   162→        \"<up to 5 quotes total, can be paraphrased but must reflect real feedback>\"\n   163→      ]\n   164→    }\n   165→  ]\n   166→```\n   167→\n   168→* Only include products that:\n   169→\n   170→  * You have **good evidence** were launched in the last 14 days, and\n   171→  * Clearly belong to the **AI coding / developer tools** space.\n   172→\n   173→* If you cannot find any products that satisfy the 14-day constraint,\n   174→  return an empty JSON array: `[]`.\n   175→\n   176→Be concise, factual, and avoid marketing fluff. Do **not** include your reasoning text\n   177→in the final answer—only the JSON.\n   178→\n   179→**File output + incremental updates requirement**\n   180→- 